# Responsive

- Adapt the interface to small screens.

- Adapt the interface to tablets.

- Adapt the interface to large screens.

## Reflow and small screens

- Under the `md` breakpoint (viewport width < 896px), when the layout reflows
  (elements stack vertically because of the resize), the page MUST become
  scrollable: all elements must remain reachable. No data or element may be
  clipped or hidden. Scroll rules and implementation: see
  `knowledge-base/global/layout.mdc` and `components/layout/app-layout.tsx`.
- Under the same breakpoint, tables MUST transform into stacked cards carrying
  ALL the column values of their rows (visible, or revealed by the card
  in-place toggle): no hidden column, no horizontal
  scroll. See `knowledge-base/components/tables.mdc` and `components/ui/user-table.tsx`.
- At `md+`, the global vertical page scroll is allowed on non-dashboard pages
  when the content genuinely requires it, while dashboard pages still fit the
  viewport and never scroll (rules: see `knowledge-base/global/layout.mdc`).

